  "source": "EAMCET 2007 (Engineering)",
  "question": "A black body radiates energy at the rate of $E$ watt/m$^2$ at a high temperature $T$ K. When the temperature is reduced to $\\dfrac{T}{2}$ K, the radiant energy is",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\dfrac{E}{2}$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$2E$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\dfrac{E}{4}$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\dfrac{E}{16}$",
      "image": ""
    }
  ],
  "answer": "D",
  "numerical_answer": "",
  "tolerance": "",
  "solution": "$E \\propto T^4$, so halving $T$ gives $\\dfrac{E}{2^4} = \\dfrac{E}{16}$.",
